# Shell scripts must be LF whatever the checkout platform does. CI runs
# .github/scripts/*.sh through bash, and a CRLF line ending there fails with
# a carriage return in every command ("command not found" on a line that
# plainly exists), which is a miserable thing to debug from a runner log.
#
# Scoped to *.sh deliberately: a repo-wide `* text=auto`, as Register has,
# would renormalise every file in the repo in one unrelated commit.
*.sh text eol=lf
